FINAL CONCLUSION:

The Zomato dataset is first cleaned by handling missing values and outliers. Categorical features such as cuisine and location are converted into numerical values using OneHotEncoder, while cost and rating are standardized using StandardScaler.

Logistic Regression and Random Forest are then trained to predict whether a restaurant has a rating above 4.0. Their ROC-AUC scores are compared to determine which model performs better.

If the high-rating class is strongly imbalanced, SMOTE is applied only to the training data. GridSearchCV is then used to find the best Random Forest values for n_estimators and max_depth.
